      "side": 1,
      "message": "yes, this is common x86 cpu architecture related data structure definitions, it\u0027s more better to put in core/minute-ia folder. :)\n\nbut i think before moving it to core/minute-ia, we need make all the definitions are unify, and all other code not re-implementing but just using the unify definitions from this single file (ia_structs.h etc).\n\njust as you mentioned, the core/minute-ia/interrupts.h already defined \u0027IDT_entry\u0027, i think at best put all x86 tables definitions including this \u0027IDT_entry\u0027 into the single unify ia_structs.h, remove the \u0027IDT_entry\u0027 defines in interrupts.h, let it using the one defined in ia_structs.h. \n\nbut for current patch, i think we at best focus on ISH PM functions, impact other parts as few as possible, especially for the basic core code of minute-ia. after this patch fully verified and merged, then we can consider to do this, make ia_structs.h more common for minute-ia and move to core/miniute-ia folder. \n@Jet and Jack, how do you think about it ?",
