      "message": "yes, that\u0027s a good question :) \naontask needs it\u0027s own IDT and can\u0027t reuse the on defined in core/init.S, and needs other x86 tables definitions, such as GDT, LDT, TSS. And I think at best we need a unify common header file (ia_structs.h etc) to define all x86 arch related tables, such as GDT, IDT, LDT, TSS and so on. and this file should be located in core/minute-ia/include folder, all other code should using the unified definitions from this header file and no re-implementing.  \n\njust as my early comments, can we do this after this patch fully verified and merged ? since at current need focus on the ISH PM functions, and at best to impact other codes as few as possible.:)      \n\n@Jet and Jack,  how do you think about it ?",
