      "writtenOn": "2019-03-20T11:56:31Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "moved ia_structs.h into core/minute-ia folder with a new CL.\n\nsome questions:\n\ncore/minute-ia/interrupts.h already defined IDT_entry:\n\n/* Interrupt descriptor entry */\nstruct IDT_entry_t {\n\tuint16_t ISR_low;\t/* Low 16 bits of handler address. */\n\tuint16_t segment_selector;\t/* Flat model means this is not changed. */\n\tuint8_t zero;\t\t/* Must be set to zero. */\n\tuint8_t flags;\t\t/* Flags for this entry. */\n\tuint16_t ISR_high;\t/* High 16 bits of handler address. */\n} __attribute__ ((packed));\ntypedef struct IDT_entry_t IDT_entry;\n\nit\u0027s coding style seems not match others, such as has capital letters, and typdedef struct xxxx_t xxxx. \n\ncan we define a unify idt_entry with same style of other tables (gdt,ldt etc) in ia_structs.h,  such as : \nunion idt_entry {\n     struct {\n         uint32_t dword_lo;\n         uint32_t dword_hi;\n     }\n     struct {\n\tuint16_t isr_lo;\t/* Low 16 bits of handler address. */\n\tuint16_t segment_selector;\t/* Flat model means this is not changed. */\n\tuint8_t zero;\t\t/* Must be set to zero. */\n\tuint8_t flags;\t\t/* Flags for this entry. */\n\tuint16_t isr_hi;\t\n     }\n}\n\nand remove the IDT_entry_t in interrupts.h ? \nthis should be a very small changes to the interrupts.c and interrupts.h. \n\nhow do you think about it? if it\u0027s ok, will update the patch.",
